CSS Properties
Justify-content:how items look along the direction of flex
align-items:how items look perpendicular to the direction of flex
by default flex is row so justify content is in row but if we set flex direction as column then justify content manages how the code looks in vertical direction
align-content:different than items as it controls how content is spaced in a flex
align-self overrides the align items of orignal flex and used to give that specific object different allignment than others
flec shrink or grow can be used to adjust the size of items relative to others when negative space is distributed.
keyframes controls the intermediate steps in an animation by defining styles for keyframes in the animation
from and to refres to the start and end of animation rather than position
